1. codewithmukesh/dotnet-claude-kit
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Project:   dotnet-claude-kit
Author:    Mukesh Murugan (codewithmukesh)
Source:    https://github.com/codewithmukesh/dotnet-claude-kit
Licence:   MIT
Pinned at: commit cd83d315986c27621da178dad73bd95d503c1540

WHAT IS DERIVED FROM IT

Every triage decision in this repository is anchored to the commit named above,
not to the project's moving `main` branch. At that commit, `dotnet-standards`
takes material from 52 of the kit's components:

  - 30 components carried as derivative works
      2  `adapt`      (kit skeleton, substance replaced with the author's own code)
      23 `keep-tweak` (kit content, edited for stack, .NET version and conventions)
      5  `keep`       (kit content taken essentially as-is)
  - 22 components merged into new files (`combine`), each carrying kit material
    into a file this plugin authors

Shipped in this release (v0.1.0):

  - `hooks/post-edit-format` — derived from the kit's `hooks/post-edit-format.sh`.
    Renamed extensionless; logic otherwise unchanged.
  - `hooks/hooks.json` — rebuilt, not copied. The kit's event map (PostToolUse on
    `Edit|Write`) is the input; the file itself is written here because the kit's
    `bash "…/x.sh"` command form cannot run on Windows and because this plugin
    ships only one of the three hooks the kit's manifest registers.
  - `hooks/README.md` — the kit's three-kinds hook taxonomy, rewritten for the
    one hook this plugin actually ships.

The remaining derived material lands in skills and reference documents in later
releases. This notice covers all of it.

A NOTE ON `CWM.RoslynNavigator`

The kit repository also contains the `CWM.RoslynNavigator` MCP server (MIT,
`PackageLicenseExpression=MIT`). `dotnet-standards` **documents** that server as
an externally installed dotnet tool — `dotnet tool install -g CWM.RoslynNavigator`
— and does not vendor, bundle or copy any part of it. It therefore creates no
separate attribution obligation; it lives in the repository this section already
covers.

