2. obra/superpowers
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Project:   superpowers
Author:    Jesse Vincent (obra)
Source:    https://github.com/obra/superpowers
Licence:   MIT
Read at:   installed version 6.2.0

WHAT IS COPIED FROM IT

  - `hooks/run-hook.cmd` — the polyglot CMD/POSIX hook wrapper. This is a copy of
    Superpowers' `hooks/run-hook.cmd`: the same heredoc structure, the same bash
    discovery order (Program Files, Program Files (x86), then `where bash`), and
    the same silent `exit /b 0` when no bash is found. Only the comments differ.

WHY IT IS COPIED RATHER THAN REFERENCED

`dotnet-standards` and Superpowers are independent plugins. Pointing this
plugin's `hooks.json` at Superpowers' internal path would couple the two and
would break the moment Superpowers is updated, moved or uninstalled. The
project's own rules forbid it, and forbid modifying any Superpowers file. So the
pattern is copied — which is exactly what creates this attribution obligation.

Nothing else from Superpowers is copied. Superpowers remains installed and
unmodified as the process layer alongside this plugin.

